{"id":"87f555d1-8619-4827-8147-e30f3014e717","article_key":"doi:10.1016/s1474-4422(26)00277-2","title":"Safety, tolerability, and efficacy of RIPK1 inhibitor, SAR443820, in amyotrophic lateral sclerosis (HIMALAYA): a multicentre, randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled, phase 2 trial","title_zh":"RIPK1抑制剂SAR443820在肌萎缩侧索硬化症（HIMALAYA）中的安全性、耐受性与疗效：一项多中心、随机、双盲、安慰剂对照、二期临床试验","doi":"10.1016/s1474-4422(26)00277-2","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/s1474-4422(26)00277-2","abstract":"BACKGROUND: RIPK1, a protein regulating inflammatory signalling and cell death, is implicated in amyotrophic lateral sclerosis (ALS) pathophysiology. SAR443820 is a selective, oral, CNS-penetrant, reversible RIPK1 inhibitor. We aimed to evaluate the safety, tolerability, and efficacy of SAR443820 in participants with ALS. METHODS: This multicentre, randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled, phase 2 trial was conducted at 63 clinical sites in 13 countries (Belgium, Canada, China, France, Germany, Italy, Japan, the Netherlands, Poland, Spain, Sweden, the UK, and the USA). Adults (aged 18-80 years) with a diagnosis of possible ALS, clinically probable ALS, clinically probable laboratory-supported ALS, or clinically definite ALS, in accordance with the revised El Escorial World Federation of Neurology criteria, were randomly assigned (2:1) by use of a stratified block design (blocks of three) to receive either 20 mg SAR443820 orally twice per day or matching placebo in the 24-week double-blind period. Randomisation was done centrally using interactive response technology and stratified by geographical region of trial site, region of ALS onset, use of riluzole, use of edaravone, and use of the combination of sodium phenylbutyrate and taurursodiol. Participants, care providers, investigators, and outcomes assessors were masked to trial intervention. The primary outcome was a change in ALS Functional Rating Scale Revised (ALSFRS-R) total score from baseline to week 24 and was calculated for all participants who had an ALSFRS-R total score available at baseline and at week 24. Safety analyses included all randomly assigned participants receiving one dose or more of trial intervention. This trial is registered with ClinicalTrials.gov (NCT05237284) and was terminated early. FINDINGS: Between April 13, 2022, and July 17, 2023, 397 participants were screened and 305 randomly assigned to SAR443820 (n=203) or placebo (n=102); six were excluded from the primary analysis due to missing baseline ALSFRS-R values. Mean age was 56·9 years (SD 11·5); 183 (60%) participants were male and 122 (40%) were female. Least squares mean change in ALSFRS-R from baseline to week 24 was -6·73 (95% CI -7·48 to -5·98) for SAR443820 group (n=169) and -6·32 (-7·36 to -5·27) for placebo group (n=87). There was no statistically significant difference between the study groups (least squares mean difference -0·41 [95% CI -1·71 to 0·88]). Participants in the SAR443820 group had higher incidence of adverse events (171 [85%] of 202 vs placebo 80 [78%] of 102) and treatment discontinuations (28 [14%] of 202 vs placebo five [5%] of 102), with elevated hepatic enzymes being the most common cause. Nine deaths occurred in the double-blind period (seven [3%] of 202 in the SAR443820 group and two [2%] of 102 in the placebo group); none was attributed to SAR443820. INTERPRETATION: SAR443820 did not show clinical benefit and was associated with higher hepatic enzyme increase, indicating that further clinical development of SAR443820 in ALS is not warranted. FUNDING: Sanofi.","abstract_zh":"背景：RIPK1是一种调节炎症信号和细胞死亡的蛋白，已被认为与肌萎缩侧索硬化症（ALS）的发病机制相关。SAR443820是一种选择性、口服、可穿透中枢神经系统、可逆的RIPK1抑制剂。本研究旨在评估SAR443820在ALS患者中的安全性、耐受性和疗效。方法：本多中心、随机、双盲、安慰剂对照、二期试验在13个国家（比利时、加拿大、中国、法国、德国、意大利、日本、荷兰、波兰、西班牙、瑞典、英国和美国）的63个临床中心进行。符合修订版El Escorial世界神经学联合会标准的18-80岁ALS疑似、临床疑似、临床疑似实验室支持或临床确诊患者被随机分配（2:1）接受每日口服20 mg SAR443820两次或匹配安慰剂，24周双盲期。随机化采用中心化交互式响应技术，并按试验地点地理区域、ALS发病区域、利鲁唑使用、依达拉奉使用以及苯丁酰钠与牛磺酸二硫酸盐组合使用进行分层。受试者、护理人员、研究者和结果评估者均对试验干预保持盲法。主要终点为24周时ALS功能评定量表修订版（ALSFRS-R）总分相对于基线的变化，计算基线和24周均有ALSFRS-R总分的所有受试者。安全性分析包括所有接受至少一次试验干预的随机分配受试者。本试验已在ClinicalTrials.gov注册（NCT05237284），并提前终止。结果：2022年4月13日至2023年7月17日期间，共筛查397名受试者，随机分配305名（SAR443820 203名，安慰剂 102名）；6名因基线ALSFRS-R缺失被排除在主要分析之外。平均年龄56.9岁（标准差11.5岁）；男性183人（60%），女性122人（40%）。SAR443820组基线至24周的最小二乘均值变化为-6.73（95%置信区间-7.48至-5.98，n=169），安慰剂组为-6.32（95%置信区间-7.36至-5.27，n=87）。两组间无统计学显著差异（最小二乘均值差异-0.41，95%置信区间-1.71至0.88）。SAR443820组不良事件发生率更高（202人中171人，85%）且停药率更高（28人，14%）相较于安慰剂组（102人中80人，78%；5人，5%），最常见的不良事件为肝酶升高。双盲期共发生9例死亡（SAR443820组7例，3%；安慰剂组2例，2%），未归因于SAR443820。结论：SAR443820未显示临床益处，且与肝酶升高相关，提示不建议继续在ALS中开展SAR443820的临床开发。资金来源：赛诺菲。","snippet":"BACKGROUND: RIPK1, a protein regulating inflammatory signalling and cell death, is implicated in amyotrophic lateral sclerosis (ALS) pathophysiology. SAR443820 is a selective, oral, CNS-penetrant, reversible RIPK1 inhibitor. We aimed to evaluate the safety, tolerability, and efficacy of SAR443820 in participants with ALS. METHODS: This multicentre, randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled, phase 2 trial was cond…","translated_at":"2026-09-10T22:37:01.804587Z","translation_model":"openai/gpt-oss-20b","source_category":"doi","article_type":"Multicenter Study","volume":"25","issue":"10","published_at":"2026-10-01T00:00:00","acquired_at":"2026-09-10T19:47:49Z","display_date":"2026-09-10T19:47:49Z","display_date_source":"acquired","online_published_at":null,"print_published_at":"2026-10-01T00:00:00","first_author":"Merit E Cudkowicz","authors_text":"Merit E Cudkowicz, Jeremy Shefner, Leonard H van den Berg, Adriano Chio, Dongsheng Fan, Julian Großkreutz, Christian Lunetta, Richard M Tsai, Ye Li, Erik Wallstroem, Li Xiong, Yixin Chen, Nazem Atassi, Kristl Claeys, Philip Van Damme, Philippe Beauchemin, Annie Dionne, Oliver Blanchard, Angela Genge, Rami Massie, Jeanne Teitelbaum, Grayson Beecher, Peter Dobrowolski, Wendy Johnston, Michael Nicolle, Christen Shoesmith, Marvin Chum, John Turnbull, Agessandro Abrahao, Antonio Saldanha De Cast